---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Faculty portal"
  path="/docs/user-guide/faculty-portal"
  description="Daily work for teaching staff — classes, attendance, grading, schedules, and student management."
>
  <p>
    The Faculty Portal is the React-based workspace for teaching staff. The
    pages available to you depend on the feature toggles your administrators
    have enabled; if an area described here is missing, ask an administrator to
    review the faculty feature toggles.
  </p>

  <h2>Dashboard and action center</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The <strong>dashboard</strong> summarizes your teaching load, upcoming classes,
      and items that need attention.
    </li>
    <li>
      The <strong>action center</strong> collects pending work — submissions to grade,
      attendance to complete, and requests awaiting your response — so you can clear
      tasks from one place.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Classes</h2>
  <p>Each of your assigned classes has its own workspace:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Posts and materials</strong> — publish announcements, lessons, and resources
      to the class stream.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Submissions</strong> — review student assignment submissions, grade
      them, and return feedback.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>People</strong> — view the enrolled roster and manage students in your
      section, including section moves where permitted.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Grading</strong> — encode and submit grades per grading period. Submitted
      grades follow the school's verification workflow before they become final.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>Class rosters and reports can be exported as PDF from the class area.</p>

  <h2>Attendance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Open an <strong>attendance session</strong> for a class meeting and mark students
      present, late, absent, or excused.
    </li>
    <li>
      Review <strong>attendance records</strong> per class and export attendance reports
      for your own records or for submission.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Schedule</h2>
  <p>The schedule area shows your teaching timetable in two views:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Agenda view</strong> — a chronological list of upcoming classes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Bird's-eye view</strong> — the full week at a glance, useful for spotting
      gaps and conflicts.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Grades</h2>
  <p>
    The grades area lists your classes per grading period. Encode scores, then
    <strong>submit</strong> them for verification. Once submitted, changes go through
    the authorized process rather than direct edits — contact your registrar if a
    submitted grade needs correction.
  </p>

  <h2>Profile and security</h2>
  <p>
    From your profile settings you can enable <strong
      >two-factor authentication</strong
    > (authenticator app or e-mail code) and register
    <strong>passkeys</strong> for faster, phishing-resistant sign-in. API keys for
    personal integrations are also managed here when permitted.
  </p>
  <div class="doc-callout doc-callout-note">
    <p class="doc-callout-label">What this does</p>
    <p>
      Enabling two-factor authentication protects student data in your classes.
      It applies to your account only and takes effect at your next sign-in.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
